      "message": "[Review from Jetski]\n\nCould we validate `schema.providers` directly inside `Attr::resolve_label_or_file` (by bounding `S::TargetRef: TargetAttrExt`) instead of threading a `validate_providers` closure through `create_ctx_fields` -\u003e `to_value` -\u003e `resolve_and_collect` -\u003e `resolve_label_or_file`?\n\nSince `attr` already depends on `providers` and defines `TargetAttrExt::has_provider` in this CL, moving `verify_providers` into `attr` (alongside `NoMatchingOutputs` and `MustProduceSingleFile`) would:\n1. Avoid the 4-layer callback plumbing, the `#[expect(clippy::too_many_arguments)]` here, and the no-op `|_, _| Ok(())` closures in the `attr` unit tests.\n2. Avoid duplicating the attribute name in the error message — currently line 150 wraps the error with ``for attribute `{name}` `` on top of `MissingRequiredProviders` (`In \u0027{attr}\u0027 attribute of \u0027{rule}\u0027 rule {target}: ...`). If we still want the rule/target context in the message, `rule::run` could attach `.with_context(...)` once around `create_ctx_fields(...)` so all attribute resolution errors share the same context format.",
