      "message": "[Review from Jetski]\n\nnit: For `providers \u003d []` (an empty list, meaning no required providers, as allowed in Bazel), this currently produces `Vec::new()` only because `ProvidersArg` tries `Either::Left` (`UnpackList\u003cUnpackList\u003c\u0026ProviderType\u003e\u003e`) before `Either::Right` (`UnpackList\u003c\u0026ProviderType\u003e`). If the `Either` variants were ever reordered, `Some(Either::Right(ps))` would produce `vec![vec![]]` instead of `vec![]`, which would subtly break `AttrSchema` equality (e.g. in `check_override`) and `validate_providers`.\n\nConsider handling `ps.items.is_empty()` explicitly in the `Either::Right` arm as well (or adding a short comment), and adding unit test cases for `providers \u003d []` and `providers \u003d [[]]` (empty group error).",
