      "message": "[Review from Jetski]\n\nWhat happens if a label attribute with `providers` points to a native GN target (defined in a `.gn` file rather than via a Starlark rule)?\n\nAs far as I can tell:\n1. `register_dependency` only adds the label to `starlark_deps_` without registering a `rust::Target` on the dependency, so when the native target finishes resolving in `Target::OnResolvedWithoutChecks`, `rust_target_` is typically still null and `execute_rule_impl` is not run.\n2. Even if the native target gets lazily registered via `CxxTarget::to_rust` -\u003e `Session::register_cxx_target` (or once `Session::get_target` supports looking up native targets), its `evaluated` `OnceCell` remains uninitialized, so `self.0.evaluated()` here will panic with `\"Should only be called on an evaluated target\"` (unlike `FakeTargetRef::has_provider`, which uses `evaluated.get().is_some_and(...)`, though native targets should presumably also expose `DefaultInfo` via `run_builtin_rule`).\n\nIf cross-referencing native GN targets from Starlark label attributes is planned for a follow-up CL, a `TODO` comment here would be helpful; otherwise we should make sure native targets do not panic here.",
